# evidence: hand-run oven cross-build of fix/869-openssl-cert-dir (a1f2518657)
# instance: i-06a3ece3530a9d4e3 (Ubuntu 24.04 arm64, c7g.16xlarge, ami-0dcf79589cb11e193)   region: us-west-2   transport: SSM send-command
# why by hand: the bake pipelines build only their pinned source branch; repointing one is a shared-infra change.
# what: install/pre_build/build phases of graviton/pipeline/buildspecs/cross-build.yml, verbatim, env copied from
#   CodeBuild project haiku-oven-cross-build (read-only: cross-tools cache + hpkg-pool from its work bucket).
#   post_build skipped: it only writes caches back to S3.
# raw -> AMI: dd of haiku-ec2.raw onto a blank 20 GiB gp3 volume (vol-0b78a10782d225f68), result dd=0,
#   then cmp of the raw file against the device, after drop_caches, result cmp=0 (byte-identical).
#   (A first conv=sparse dd did NOT match, cmp differ at byte 16777217: the device read back non-zero bytes there where the raw file is all zero, so the sparse skip left stale bytes. The full dd above replaced it.)
#   snapshot snap-006796de8291f79d4 -> register-image ami-00815d331a64e02ac, with the same arm64/uefi/ena/hvm/xvda flags
#   as graviton/pipeline/scripts/import-and-register.sh. NOT tagged candidate, never promoted.
# log: \r progress lines of 'aws s3' turned into newlines, and 'Completed ... remaining' progress lines dropped
# ---- driver: crossbuild.sh ----
# | #!/bin/bash
# | # Reproduces the oven CodeBuild cross-build (install, pre_build, build phases of
# | # graviton/pipeline/buildspecs/cross-build.yml, verbatim) on an Ubuntu 24.04 arm64
# | # EC2 instance (each command run the CodeBuild way, see runphase.py), for branch fix/869-openssl-cert-dir. post_build is skipped: it only
# | # writes caches back to S3. Env values are the haiku-oven-cross-build project's.
# | set -euo pipefail
# | export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
# | export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-west-2 HAIKU_REVISION=hrev59996 HG_SSH_DIR=/opt/haiku/ssh
